[2026.10.30-14.00.00:000][100]LogNodeShuffle: Display: LAYOUTDUMP-LEGEND: Positions are world centimetres. Entry lines give each layout entry's CURRENT saved location, after any redeal or resettle, not the spot first rolled; inactive entries are never spawned and are not dealt spots; notNew counts entries that are original level nodes, not dealt by the mod.
[2026.10.30-14.00.00:000][100]LogNodeShuffle: Display: LAYOUTDUMP-LEGEND: Purity is the enum integer (0 impure, 1 normal, 2 pure, 3 unset); live means a spawned actor for the entry is valid in this session right now; rayCasted means the entry was settled by a trace at some earlier time.
[2026.10.30-14.00.00:000][100]LogNodeShuffle: Display: LAYOUTDUMP-LEGEND: Well lines come from the separate well layout; their position source names which saved location was printed (placed core, dealt destination, RWG claim, vanilla core, or none). Original lines print the record's true location when set, else its recorded location, and the purity of the layout entry sharing its level path or minus one when no entry matches.
[2026.10.30-14.00.00:000][100]LogNodeShuffle: Display: LAYOUTDUMP-LEGEND: Grid lines cover the API deal square in 1000 m cells from its minimum corner; edge cells may extend past it. Each cell samples a centred lattice through the height API only: land counts samples passing the RWG reject predicate at the API surface, dealable counts samples passing the dealer's whole land chain (outside, reject predicate, slope). Spacing and the cave quota are not part of dealable.
[2026.10.30-14.00.00:000][100]LogNodeShuffle: Display: LAYOUTDUMP-LEGEND: The end line repeats every count beside what the begin line announced; countsMatch is one only when all of them agree. The dump runs in a single frame; it prints one line per layout entry, well core, original record and grid cell that the begin line announces, plus the begin, legend, end and chat lines.
[2026.10.30-14.00.00:000][100]LogNodeShuffle: Display: LAYOUTDUMP-LEGEND: Grid lines print only when this session's sea, void and killbox checks have all finished; otherwise the grid count is zero. Latch masks add 1 sea usable, 2 void usable, 4 killbox known, 8 sea checked, 16 void checked, 32 killbox checked.
